chronymon (1.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * COASTING only while the selected source has answered none of its
    last 8 polls.  1.2.0 said so whenever four update intervals passed
    without a clock update, which an NTP server missing a few long
    polls does with nothing wrong; 1.2.0 was withdrawn.
  * A long reference name keeps to its place: two cells in the strip,
    cut short past them, and on the kiosk its line shrinks to fit.
  * Otherwise as 1.2.0, below.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:31:32 -0700

chronymon (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Upgrading: the database goes to schema 7 on first open, and 1.1.0's
    daemon will not open it again.  chrony.conf is now read as strictly
    as chronyd reads it; one that cannot be read leaves the last good
    one in use, and the Journal and every page say so.
  * --pps watches PPS edges where the kernel sees them, /dev/ppsN or a
    PTP clock's pin, and journals pulses lost, flapping and down.
  * --gpsd records each receiver's fix, satellites and dilutions of
    precision, and journals fixes lost and regained and gpsd down.
  * Steps on the clock that makestep's rule did not say are journaled
    as clock_step, a rule's step the clock did not take as step_unseen.
  * What is wrong now stays on screen while it lasts: on the kiosk, a
    large line each under the sync state, the panel edged red or amber;
    on every other page, pills after LIVE, the strip edged likewise.
    The kiosk says COASTING while chronyd has gone four update
    intervals without updating the clock, and ON BACKUPS while it is
    on other than its own refclocks; the strip says so too.
  * Reference changes say from what to what, a refclock by its
    reference ID, and the kiosk's list shows each event's detail.
  * The daemon starts whenever chrony starts.
  * Betas are GitHub pre-releases, never in the APT repository.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:45:00 -0700

