chronymon (1.2.0~beta.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Beta.  The database goes to schema 7 on first open, and 1.1.0's
    daemon will not open it again.
  * chrony.conf is read as strictly as chronyd reads it, includes and
    all; on an error the last good one is kept and the Journal says so.
    `--chrony-config none` for a chronyd configured otherwise.
  * The daemon starts whenever chrony starts.
  * --pps watches PPS edges where the kernel sees them, /dev/ppsN or a
    PTP clock's pin, and journals pulses lost, flapping and down; the
    Refclocks page shades the spans.
  * --gpsd records each receiver's fix, satellites and dilutions of
    precision, journals fixes lost and regained, and charts them on
    the Refclocks page.
  * Steps on the clock that makestep's rule did not say, chronyc
    makestep, -R, a leap second or another program, are journaled as
    clock_step; a rule's step the clock did not take as step_unseen.
  * Betas are GitHub pre-releases, never in the APT repository.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:58:03 -0700

